abstract: >
  CallingGraph Unfolding for AI Coding (CGU) studies how a folded
  functional CallingGraph can be selectively unfolded into localized
  structural possibilities for design-time planning, AI coding execution,
  runtime validation, and evidence-bounded certification.

  CGU v1.0 focuses strictly on Function-only CallingGraph structure.
  It introduces CallingGraph Folding, Trigger-Localized Unfolding,
  Design-Time CallingGraphs, Structural Wargaming, Realized CallingGraphs,
  the Unfolding Gap, Differential Unfolding, confidence-based certification,
  and the CallingGraph as an AI Coding Structural Control Plane.

  The framework moves CallingGraph from a passive post-coding analysis
  artifact toward an operational structural object that can participate
  across the software lifecycle:

  Design -> Unfold -> Simulate -> Dispatch -> Code -> Fold ->
  Compare -> Certify -> Learn.

